# Testing rules

Every behavior change needs tests. Revolutionary concept, apparently.

## Narrow checks

Run the narrowest relevant test while iterating:

```bash
pytest -q tests/test_demo_resampling.py
pytest -q tests/test_demo_contact.py
pytest -q tests/test_demo_mocap.py
pytest -q tests/test_demo.py
pytest -q tests/test_demo_sync.py
```

## Full checks

Before considering a task done:

```bash
python3 -m compileall -q src/retarget examples
pytest -q
uv run mypy
```

`uv run mypy` is strict; the typed deep chain must stay clean. Cover the deep
chain with `assert_type` (see `tests/test_demo_container.py` and
`tests/test_typed_deep_chain.py`).

## Resampling tests

For resampling behavior, cover:

- input timestamp validation;
- empty timestamp behavior;
- nearest/previous index behavior;
- tie/clamp behavior;
- full track behavior;
- view behavior;
- `output_timestamps` relabeling;
- source-time sampling vs output-time labeling.

## Sync tests

For sync behavior, cover:

- connected non-star graph;
- duplicate directed/undirected edge rejection;
- missing tracks;
- pairwise alignment estimation;
- graph composition;
- reverse-edge inversion;
- one-shot sync-and-resample workflow.

